{"task_id": "Mbpp/16", "solution": "import re\n\ndef text_lowercase_underscore(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns true if the input string contains sequences of lowercase letters\n    joined with an underscore and false otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The regex pattern checks for:\n    # ^             - start of the string\n    # [a-z]+        - one or more lowercase letters (the initial sequence)\n    # _             - an underscore (the first required joiner)\n    # [a-z]+        - one or more lowercase letters (the second required sequence)\n    # (?:_[a-z]+)*  - a non-capturing group that can repeat zero or more times:\n    #   _           - an underscore\n    #   [a-z]+      - one or more lowercase letters (subsequent sequences)\n    # $             - end of the string\n    # This pattern ensures that the string consists of only lowercase letters\n    # and underscores, with at least one underscore, and that sequences of\n    # lowercase letters are properly joined by single underscores.\n    return bool(re.fullmatch(r\"^[a-z]+_[a-z]+(?:_[a-z]+)*$\", input_string))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "```python\ndef check(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    Uses helper functions for modularity.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def reverse_number(num):\n        \"\"\"Reverses the digits of a given number.\"\"\"\n        s = str(num)\n        return int(s[::-1])\n\n    def calculate_twice_reverse(reversed_num):\n        \"\"\"Calculates twice the value of a reversed number.\"\"\"\n        return reversed_num * 2\n\n    def compare_with_one_less(original, twice_reverse):\n        \"\"\"Compares original number with one less than twice the reversed number.\"\"\"\n        return original == twice_reverse - 1\n\n    reversed_num = reverse_number(number)\n    twice_reversed = calculate_twice_reverse(reversed_num)\n    return compare_with_one_less(number, twice_reversed)\n```"}
