{"task_id": "Mbpp/58", "solution": "def opposite_Signs(num1: int, num2: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if two integers have opposite signs.\n    Returns True if one is positive and the other is negative, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _get_sign(number: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Determines the sign of an integer as a string ('positive', 'negative', 'zero').\"\"\"\n        if number > 0:\n            return \"positive\"\n        elif number < 0:\n            return \"negative\"\n        else:\n            return \"zero\"\n\n    def _are_opposite_signs(sign1: str, sign2: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Compares two sign strings to check if they are opposite.\"\"\"\n        return (sign1 == \"positive\" and sign2 == \"negative\") or \\\n               (sign1 == \"negative\" and sign2 == \"positive\")\n\n    sign1 = _get_sign(num1)\n    sign2 = _get_sign(num2)\n    return _are_opposite_signs(sign1, sign2)"}
