{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number, representing the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n    Raises ValueError if n is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize the Bell triangle with B(0)\n    # bell_triangle[i][0] will store B(i)\n    bell_triangle = [[1]] \n\n    # Build the triangle row by row up to n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        current_row = [bell_triangle[i-1][-1]] # First element of current row is the last of the previous row\n        \n        # Calculate subsequent elements in the current row: A[i][j] = A[i][j-1] + A[i-1][j-1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            current_row.append(current_row[j-1] + bell_triangle[i-1][j-1])\n        \n        bell_triangle.append(current_row)\n    \n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row\n    return bell_triangle[n][0]"}
