{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    a(n, m) counts permutations of {1, ..., n} with m ascents.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _combinations(N, K):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(N, K).\"\"\"\n        if K < 0 or K > N:\n            return 0\n        if K == 0 or K == N:\n            return 1\n        if K > N // 2:\n            K = N - K\n        \n        res = 1\n        for i in range(K):\n            res = res * (N - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    # Eulerian numbers are defined for non-negative n and m.\n    # Return 0 for invalid negative inputs, consistent with combinatorial contexts.\n    if n < 0 or m < 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Base case: A(0,0) = 1 (empty permutation has 0 ascents), A(0,m>0) = 0.\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 if m == 0 else 0\n\n    # Calculate using the explicit formula: A(n, m) = sum_{j=0}^{m} (-1)^j * C(n+1, j) * (m+1-j)^n\n    result = 0\n    for j in range(m + 1):\n        term_sign = (-1)**j\n        comb_val = _combinations(n + 1, j)\n        power_val = (m + 1 - j)**n\n        \n        result += term_sign * comb_val * power_val\n        \n    return result"}
