{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def sum_of_common_divisors(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of common divisors for two given integers.\n    This function delegates to helper functions for divisor calculation, common divisor identification, and summation.\n    \"\"\"\n    def get_divisors(n: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates all positive divisors for a given integer n.\"\"\"\n        divs = []\n        for i in range(1, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                divs.append(i)\n                if i * i != n:\n                    divs.append(n // i)\n        return sorted(divs)\n\n    def find_common_divisors(divisors1: list[int], divisors2: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Identifies common divisors between two lists of divisors.\"\"\"\n        return sorted(list(set(divisors1) & set(divisors2)))\n\n    def sum_divisors(divisors: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the arithmetic sum of a list of divisors.\"\"\"\n        return sum(divisors)\n\n    divisors1 = get_divisors(num1)\n    divisors2 = get_divisors(num2)\n    common_divs = find_common_divisors(divisors1, divisors2)\n    return sum_divisors(common_divs)"}
