{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(array: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zero values to non-zero values in an array of integers.\n    Returns 0.0 if there are no non-zero values to avoid division by zero.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _count_zeros(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of zero values in the array.\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        for x in arr:\n            if x == 0:\n                count += 1\n        return count\n\n    def _count_non_zeros(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of non-zero values in the array.\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        for x in arr:\n            if x != 0:\n                count += 1\n        return count\n\n    def _calculate_ratio(zeros: int, non_zeros: int) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zeros to non-zeros, returning 0.0 if no non-zeros.\"\"\"\n        if non_zeros == 0:\n            return 0.0\n        return float(zeros) / non_zeros\n\n    num_zeros = _count_zeros(array)\n    num_non_zeros = _count_non_zeros(array)\n\n    return _calculate_ratio(num_zeros, num_non_zeros)"}
