{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, ...) of the given number to 1.\n    This uses a bitwise OR operation with a mask that has 1s at even positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    # A 64-bit mask where all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, ...) are 1.\n    # In binary, this pattern is ...01010101.\n    even_bit_mask = 0x5555555555555555\n    \n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set the specified even bits to 1.\n    # If an even bit in 'number' is already 1, it remains 1. If it's 0, it becomes 1.\n    return number | even_bit_mask"}
