{"task_id": "Mbpp/279", "solution": "def _validate_input(n: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validate that the input n is a positive integer.\n    Raises TypeError or ValueError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\ndef is_num_decagonal(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the nth decagonal number using formula n * (4n - 3)\n\n    Args:\n        n (int): Positive integer representing position in sequence\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The nth decagonal number\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer\n        TypeError: If n is not an integer\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(n)\n    return n * (4 * n - 3)"}
