{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(integer: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    Uses helper functions for counting digit frequencies and validating them.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _count_digit_frequency(num: int) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Counts the frequency of each digit in the given integer.\"\"\"\n        freq_map = {str(i): 0 for i in range(10)}\n        num_str = str(num)\n        for char_digit in num_str:\n            freq_map[char_digit] += 1\n        return freq_map\n\n    def _is_frequency_valid(freq_dict: dict) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Validates if each digit's frequency is less than or equal to the digit's value.\"\"\"\n        for digit_str, frequency in freq_dict.items():\n            digit_val = int(digit_str)\n            if frequency > digit_val and frequency > 0: # frequency > 0 check handles digits not present\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    frequency_map = _count_digit_frequency(integer)\n    return _is_frequency_valid(frequency_map)"}
