{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n'th Lucas number using an iterative approach.\n    The Lucas sequence starts with L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n)=L(n-1)+L(n-2) for n>=2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 2, 1  # L(0) and L(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_lucas = a + b\n        a = b\n        b = next_lucas\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/388", "solution": "def _validate_input(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates if n is a positive integer.\"\"\"\n    return n > 0\n\ndef _calculate_highest_power(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the highest power of 2 less than or equal to n.\"\"\"\n    power = 1\n    while power * 2 <= n:\n        power *= 2\n    return power\n\ndef highest_Power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\n    Returns 0 if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_input(n):\n        return 0\n    return _calculate_highest_power(n)"}
