{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts an array using the shell sort algorithm by performing gapped insertion sort passes.\n    Returns a new sorted array in ascending order without modifying the original input.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    arr_copy = arr[:]  # Create a copy to ensure immutability of the original array\n\n    def _generate_gap_sequence(length: int) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Generates a common gap sequence for Shell Sort, typically halving.\"\"\"\n        gaps = []\n        gap = length // 2\n        while gap > 0:\n            gaps.append(gap)\n            gap //= 2\n        return gaps\n\n    def _shell_sort_with_gap(array: list, current_gap: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Performs a single pass of gapped insertion sort on the array.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(current_gap, len(array)):\n            temp = array[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift elements that are 'current_gap' positions apart\n            while j >= current_gap and array[j - current_gap] > temp:\n                array[j] = array[j - current_gap]\n                j -= current_gap\n            array[j] = temp\n\n    # Generate gaps and apply gapped insertion sort for each gap\n    gaps = _generate_gap_sequence(n)\n    for gap in gaps:\n        _shell_sort_with_gap(arr_copy, gap)\n\n    return arr_copy"}
