{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the first n Perrin numbers.\n    The Perrin sequence is defined by P(n) = P(n-2) + P(n-3) with P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 3\n    if n == 2:\n        return 3\n\n    # Initialize the first few Perrin numbers and their sum\n    perrin = [3, 0, 2]\n    current_sum = 5  # P(0) + P(1) + P(2) = 3 + 0 + 2 = 5\n\n    # Extend the perrin list and update sum for n > 2\n    for i in range(3, n):\n        next_perrin = perrin[i-2] + perrin[i-3]\n        perrin.append(next_perrin)\n        current_sum += next_perrin\n    \n    return current_sum"}
