{"task_id": "Mbpp/454", "solution": "def text_match_wordz(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the input string contains any word that includes the character 'z'.\n    Punctuation marks act as word separators. Case-sensitive.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # --- StringProcessor components (defined inline per design context) ---\n    # Common punctuation characters. Spaces are not included as separators per \"Treats punctuation marks as word separators\".\n    _PUNCTUATION_CHARS = '!\"#$%&\\'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\]^_`{|}~'\n\n    def _is_punctuation(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a character is a defined punctuation mark.\"\"\"\n        return char in _PUNCTUATION_CHARS\n\n    def _split_by_punctuation(text: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Splits the input string into words using punctuation as separators.\"\"\"\n        words = []\n        current_word_chars = []\n        for char in text:\n            if _is_punctuation(char):\n                if current_word_chars: # If there's a word being built, add it\n                    words.append(\"\".join(current_word_chars))\n                    current_word_chars = []\n            else: # This character is part of a word\n                current_word_chars.append(char)\n        \n        # Add any remaining word after the loop\n        if current_word_chars:\n            words.append(\"\".join(current_word_chars))\n        \n        return words\n\n    # --- WordAnalyzer components (defined inline per design context) ---\n    _TARGET_CHAR = 'z'\n\n    def _contains_character(word: str, char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a word contains the specified character.\"\"\"\n        return char in word\n\n    def _is_valid_word(word: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Validates if a word is non-empty.\"\"\"\n        return bool(word)\n\n    # --- TextMatcher orchestration (main logic) ---\n    words = _split_by_punctuation(input_string)\n\n    for word in words:\n        if _is_valid_word(word) and _contains_character(word, _TARGET_CHAR):\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
