{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within the given array.\n    Uses dynamic programming to track current maximum and minimum products.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = array[0]\n    current_max_prod = array[0]\n    current_min_prod = array[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(array)):\n        num = array[i]\n\n        # Store current_max_prod before it's updated, as it's needed for current_min_prod calculation\n        prev_max_prod = current_max_prod\n\n        # The new current_max_prod can be the number itself, or num multiplied by previous max_prod,\n        # or num multiplied by previous min_prod (if num is negative, flipping min to max).\n        current_max_prod = max(num, prev_max_prod * num, current_min_prod * num)\n        # The new current_min_prod can be the number itself, or num multiplied by previous max_prod,\n        # or num multiplied by previous min_prod.\n        current_min_prod = min(num, prev_max_prod * num, current_min_prod * num)\n\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max_prod)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
