{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "def max_product(arr: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product formed by multiplying numbers of an increasing subsequence.\n    Uses dynamic programming where dp[i] stores the maximum product of an\n    increasing subsequence ending with arr[i].\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0.0\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Initialize dp array. dp[i] will store the maximum product of an\n    # increasing subsequence ending with arr[i]. Each element arr[i]\n    # itself forms an increasing subsequence with product arr[i].\n    dp = [float(x) for x in arr]\n\n    # Initialize the overall maximum product with the maximum single-element product.\n    # This covers cases where only single-element subsequences or no extensions are possible.\n    max_overall_product = max(dp)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            # If arr[i] can extend an increasing subsequence ending at arr[j]\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                # Update dp[i] if extending the subsequence ending at arr[j]\n                # yields a larger product than existing options for dp[i].\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] * arr[i])\n        # After computing dp[i], update the overall maximum product\n        # because dp[i] might be the maximum product found so far.\n        max_overall_product = max(max_overall_product, dp[i])\n\n    return max_overall_product"}
