{"task_id": "Mbpp/563", "solution": "def extract_values(input_string: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts values enclosed within double quotation marks from a string.\n    Returns a list of these extracted values, excluding the quotation marks.\n    \"\"\"\n    extracted = []\n    in_quote = False\n    start_value_index = -1\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        if char == '\"':\n            if not in_quote:\n                # Found an opening double quote\n                in_quote = True\n                start_value_index = i + 1\n            else:\n                # Found a closing double quote\n                in_quote = False\n                # If we have a valid start index, extract the content\n                if start_value_index != -1:\n                    extracted.append(input_string[start_value_index:i])\n                start_value_index = -1  # Reset for the next potential quoted value\n\n    return extracted"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/567", "solution": "def issort_list(input_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check whether a specified list is sorted in ascending order.\n    Returns True if the list is sorted, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if input_list[i] > input_list[i + 1]:\n            return False\n    return True"}
