{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef two_unique_nums(input_list: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove duplicate numbers from input list, returning only numbers that appear exactly once.\n    Preserves the original order of unique numbers as they first appeared.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for num in input_list:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    result = []\n    for num in input_list:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            result.append(num)\n\n    return result"}
