{"task_id": "Mbpp/585", "solution": "def expensive_items(dataset: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n most expensive items in a given dataset.\n    Items are sorted by price in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not dataset or n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Sort items by price in descending order\n    sorted_items = sorted(dataset, key=lambda item: item['price'], reverse=True)\n\n    # Return the top n items, or all items if n exceeds dataset size\n    return sorted_items[:n]"}
