{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using the Bell triangle method.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Initialize Bell triangle\n    bell = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # First element of the triangle\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Bell triangle\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # First column is last element of previous row\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Other elements are sum of element left and element top-left\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i-1][j-1] + bell[i][j-1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row\n    return bell[n][0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/607", "solution": "import re\n\ndef find_literals(input_string: str, regex_pattern: str) -> tuple[str, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Search for regex pattern in string and return match with indices.\n    Raises ValueError if no match is found, TypeError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_string, str) or not isinstance(regex_pattern, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both input_string and regex_pattern must be strings.\")\n\n    match = re.search(regex_pattern, input_string)\n\n    if match:\n        return (match.group(0), match.start(), match.end())\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"No match found for the given pattern.\")"}
