{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "import math\n\ndef wind_chill(wind_velocity: float, temperature: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index given wind velocity in km/h and temperature in Celsius.\n    The result is rounded up to the next integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert wind velocity from km/h to m/s for the formula\n    # 1 km/h = 1000m / 3600s = 5/18 m/s\n    wind_velocity_ms = wind_velocity * (5 / 18)\n\n    # The standard formula for wind chill index (in Celsius, with velocity in m/s)\n    # is T_wc = 13.12 + 0.6215 * T - 11.37 * V^0.16 + 0.3965 * T * V^0.16\n    # This formula is often simplified or represented in different units.\n    # The given design context does not specify the exact formula to use, but implies\n    # a \"standard meteorological formula\". A common one for Celsius and km/h is:\n    # WC = 13.12 + 0.6215*T - 11.37*V^0.16 + 0.3965*T*V^0.16\n    # where T is temperature in Celsius and V is wind velocity in km/h.\n\n    # Calculate the wind chill using the formula based on temperature in Celsius\n    # and wind velocity in km/h.\n    # This formula is commonly used for temperature in Celsius and wind speed in km/h.\n    # Source: Environment Canada, commonly cited wind chill formula.\n    wind_chill_index = 13.12 + 0.6215 * temperature - 11.37 * (wind_velocity ** 0.16) + 0.3965 * temperature * (wind_velocity ** 0.16)\n\n    # Round the calculated result to the next integer (ceiling).\n    return math.ceil(wind_chill_index)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list using the heap sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    arr = list(input_list)  # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Helper function to heapify a subtree rooted at index i\n    # heap_size is the size of the logical heap within the array\n    def _heapify(arr, heap_size, i):\n        largest = i  # Initialize largest as root\n        left = 2 * i + 1  # left child index\n        right = 2 * i + 2  # right child index\n\n        # If left child exists and is greater than current largest\n        if left < heap_size and arr[left] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = left\n\n        # If right child exists and is greater than current largest\n        if right < heap_size and arr[right] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = right\n\n        # If largest is not root, swap and recursively heapify the affected sub-tree\n        if largest != i:\n            arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]\n            _heapify(arr, heap_size, largest)\n\n    # Helper function to build a max heap from the array\n    def _build_max_heap(arr, heap_size):\n        # Iterate from the last non-leaf node down to the first node (index 0)\n        for i in range(heap_size // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n            _heapify(arr, heap_size, i)\n\n    # Build a max heap from the array\n    _build_max_heap(arr, n)\n\n    # One by one extract elements from the heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        # Move current root (maximum element) to the end of the unsorted part\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]\n        # Call heapify on the reduced heap\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)\n\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/639", "solution": "def sample_nam(names: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Process a list of names by filtering out names starting with lowercase letters\n    and calculating the sum of the remaining names' character lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    def is_valid_name(name: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a name starts with an uppercase letter.\"\"\"\n        return len(name) > 0 and 'A' <= name[0] <= 'Z'\n\n    def filter_valid_names(names_list: list) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Filters names, keeping only those that start with an uppercase letter.\"\"\"\n        return [name for name in names_list if is_valid_name(name)]\n\n    def calculate_length_sum(names_list: list) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of character lengths for a list of names.\"\"\"\n        return sum(len(name) for name in names_list)\n\n    filtered_names = filter_valid_names(names)\n    total_length = calculate_length_sum(filtered_names)\n    return total_length"}
