{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "def reverse_Array_Upto_K(array: list, position: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the elements of an array from index 0 up to a given position (exclusive).\n    Returns a new array with the reversed segment and the rest of the array unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n    \n    # Ensure position is within valid bounds: 0 to len(array)\n    # The problem description implies 0 < position <= len(array) for meaningful reversal.\n    # If position is 0, nothing is reversed. If position >= len(array), the whole array is reversed.\n    k = min(max(0, position), len(array))\n    \n    # Slice the array into the part to be reversed and the part to remain unchanged\n    part_to_reverse = array[:k]\n    remaining_part = array[k:]\n    \n    # Reverse the first part\n    reversed_part = part_to_reverse[::-1]\n    \n    # Concatenate the reversed part with the remaining part\n    return reversed_part + remaining_part"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/643", "solution": "import re\n\ndef text_match_wordz_middle(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates word parsing and checks if any word contains 'z' in its middle.\n    Words are considered sequences of alphabetic characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _parse_words(input_string: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Extracts alphabetic words from the input string.\"\"\"\n        return re.findall(r'[a-zA-Z]+', input_string)\n\n    def _has_middle_z(word: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a single word contains 'z' in middle positions (not first or last).\"\"\"\n        if len(word) < 3:  # A word needs at least 3 characters for a 'middle' position\n            return False\n        return 'z' in word[1:-1]\n\n    words = _parse_words(input_string)\n    for word in words:\n        if _has_middle_z(word):\n            return True\n    return False"}
