{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list, positions):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of positions, returning a new list.\n    Handles empty lists and rotations greater than list length using modulo arithmetic.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    effective_positions = positions % n\n\n    if effective_positions == 0:\n        return list(input_list) # Return a copy to ensure immutability even if no rotation happens\n\n    # The last 'effective_positions' elements move to the front\n    # The remaining 'n - effective_positions' elements follow\n    return input_list[n - effective_positions:] + input_list[:n - effective_positions]"}
